# Code owners
#
# GitHub adds the listed owner as a reviewer on any pull request touching a
# matching path. This file, the `Owner:` header inside each document, and the
# table in docs/documentation.md §2 must be kept in step — three places is two
# too many, but it is what the tooling requires.
#
# STATUS 2026-08-02: the team is not yet formed, so every rule below is
# commented out. Uncommenting them with real GitHub handles is a kick-off task,
# tracked alongside filling in the `Owner:` headers. `tools/check-docs.py` warns
# on every unowned document until then, deliberately.
#
# Replace @tech-lead, @client, @designer with real
# handles. Do not use a team handle: teams do not notice that a document is
# stale; people do.

